{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1381158-describing-the-underworld","id":1381158,"title":"Describing the Underworld","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-04-13T18:16:05-07:00","id":1381158,"title":"Describing the Underworld","content":"I picked up the Compasses of Terrestrial and Celestial Directions in the Storytellers' Vault Exalted Sale, and I've been reading CoCD: Underworld. One thing I can't find is a description is how the Underworld looks and feels, particularly to a living visitor. The inhabitants are referred to as ghosts, but do they look and/or feel ghostly (translucent and insubstantial)? What about the terrain, and buildings?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1856-hakkonen","name":"Hakkonen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-13T18:45:04-07:00","id":1381170,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hakkonen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1381158-describing-the-underworld#post1381158\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I picked up the Compasses of Terrestrial and Celestial Directions in the Storytellers' Vault Exalted Sale, and I've been reading CoCD: Underworld.</div> </div> </div> </div>Keep in mind that 3e's Underworld is intended to be markedly different from 2e's Underworld. It can vary from dull gray wastes or toxic hellscapes to vivid and colorful paradises, all separated by a dark and dangerous sea.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hakkonen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1381158-describing-the-underworld#post1381158\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing I can't find is a description is how the Underworld looks and feels, particularly to a living visitor.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, at least in 2e, a lot of the traits you saw in shadowlands were either the same or even exaggerated in their adjacent Underworld territories. Green fire that is only extinguished by sunlight, black unreflective stone that naturally bears the marks of design. The scarcity of animal life, the terrible nightmares, weather quickly shifting from dead air to storms of unusual strength, raindrops often mixed with blood or ash or bits of bone or even quicksilver.<br /> <br /> &quot;This,&quot; the Deathlords say, &quot;is the rotting flesh of dead gods, shed from their bodies as they lie unquiet in their tombs beneath the world.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hakkonen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1381158-describing-the-underworld#post1381158\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The inhabitants are referred to as ghosts, but do they look and/or feel ghostly (translucent and insubstantial)?</div> </div> </div> </div>They look ghostly, in the sense of looking like someone who's died; ghosts tend to bear the mark of whatever killed them in life, and moreover, are capable of moliating themselves into fantastical shapes. But they are neither translucent nor insubstantial in the Underworld.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hakkonen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1381158-describing-the-underworld#post1381158\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What about the terrain, and buildings?\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>At least in 2e, the Underworld came into existence being <i>largely </i>analogous to Creation in terms of terrain - if a mountain range was present in Creation, it would exist in the Underworld. Cities in the Underworld would tend to be situated fairly closely to their Creation counterparts, given how a person's ghost shows up in the Underworld analogue to where the person died. Though the cities would probably hew fairly different in design given how two neighbors who both built their own houses might have a five hundred year age difference.<br /> <br /> \u200bGiven the extreme wealth available to those in the Underworld who receive worship from their ancestors, there's also going to be more of a trend toward opulence; a son who burns a hand-carved miniature boat for his deceased father might generate a full-sized sailing vessel in the lands of the dead, and sacrificing horses for his tomb creates tireless steeds in the afterlife; a basket of apples left at his grave creates a source of food that never goes empty in the Underworld.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 04-13-2020, 11:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-14T01:06:33-07:00","id":1381242,"title":"","content":"The description for ghosts is given in the Exalted (Second Edition).<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>pg315</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ghosts appear as they did in life, though lacking any infirmities they might have once possessed, with the clothes of their station, any grave goods they were buried with and the marks of death visible upon them. Many ghosts are beautiful in a distant, chill way. (The violet tinge of drowning or the red second mouth of a cut throat are easy to overlook.) Ghosts who are beginning to fade away into Lethe\u2019s embrace are quite, pallid\u2014almost translucent\u2014while those who are recently dead or are clinging with stubborn will to their existence might look almost alive, full of certainty and lifelike eagerness.</div> </div> </div> </div>Some further details may be found in the Books of Sorcery V: The Rolls of Glorious Divinity II.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-14T07:27:33-07:00","id":1381316,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1381158-describing-the-underworld?p=1381170#post1381170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bGiven the extreme wealth available to those in the Underworld who receive worship from their ancestors, there's also going to be more of a trend toward opulence; a son who burns a hand-carved miniature boat for his deceased father might generate a full-sized sailing vessel in the lands of the dead, and sacrificing horses for his tomb creates tireless steeds in the afterlife; a basket of apples left at his grave creates a source of food that never goes empty in the Underworld.</div> </div> </div> </div>That last bit raises a question: can the living eat the food of the Underworld? Does something terrible happen if they try?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1856-hakkonen","name":"Hakkonen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-14T08:38:18-07:00","id":1381330,"title":"","content":"It's not nourishing for the living (or, well, the dead, but that doesn't matter), so you'll starve.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-14T09:11:10-07:00","id":1381340,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hakkonen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1381158-describing-the-underworld?p=1381316#post1381316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That last bit raises a question: can the living eat the food of the Underworld?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't recall honestly.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hakkonen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1381158-describing-the-underworld?p=1381316#post1381316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does something terrible happen if they try?</div> </div> </div> </div>Keep in mind that there's gonna be logistical problems with feeding Underworld food to the living. Such a basket would only be self-replenishing, if memory serves, in the possession of the one to whom the apples were offered; moreover, such treasures are destroyed forever by the light of Creation's sun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 04-14-2020, 12:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-14T09:49:41-07:00","id":1381354,"title":"","content":"The Underworld is also a really big place, and not really bound by the same rules as Creation, so there's a lot of possible variability. You might have some areas that are twisted with madness, that look like Halloween Town from the Nightmare Before Christmas or even more bizarre. Some places might be slowly steaming away into nothingness, or just really quiet and maybe not so bad. It's the land of the dead though, and the living don't belong there, so few places should really be that comfy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}